Rule 2 (v_2 should be a valid dimension of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= −1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) − 1

Rule 18 (input tensor is empty or only contains non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≥ 0

Rule 16 (shape alignment for matrix multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, 0))

Rule 17 (primitive type variable must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0

